# GitHub smart answer

The GitHub smart-answer variant uses version-controlled logic and content for more complex decision trees or calculations. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/smart-answer/github-smart-answer/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

If a future household diagnostic guide needs branching rules, keep those rules in reviewed source with examples for every outcome. Separate logic from explanatory copy. A deterministic answer should cite the inputs and assumptions that produced it.

## Structure and behaviour

Define input types, units, unknown states and boundaries before rendering questions. Test every branch, backtracking and changed answers. A calculation must preserve the underlying measurement semantics and report any approximation; a design template is not authority to invent a formula.

## Home Assistant boundary

This project does not install the government’s Ruby smart-answer engine or introduce a diagnostic calculator. The examples are explicit decision documentation, with no service calls or inferred fault diagnosis. Use a simpler written guide unless the extra logic demonstrably helps.

## Decision rule record

A readable rule specification rather than an unimplemented calculator.

